invariant: INV-38
file: tls.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh writable_len
reason: ch_writable_len counts each record one byte shorter than
  rec_seal writes it, so for some caps its answer's records are longer
  than cap, and a caller's send that takes cap bytes fails and kills the
  session. The writable_len harness writes the answer through the real
  ch_write and requires what it sends to fit cap.

--- old
    size_t overhead = (whole + 1) * REC_OVERHEAD;
--- new
    size_t overhead = (whole + 1) * (REC_OVERHEAD - 1);
